c(1, "header lines 1-5; §2.1 table (verbatim); §2.2 table (verbatim)", "positioning", "Ultiself | Self-Improvement (App Store ID 1476563238) by Ultiself Corporation (com.nekritin.ultiself) — a habit tracker branded as self-improvement and biohacking: a library of explained habits (sleep, focus, mood, energy) with sources, daily check-off and day rating, reminders, prebuilt routines, statistics, a journal, sleep tools, courses and 'mind movies', AI-assisted plans in 2026; most reviewers arrive via a social-media ad → web questionnaire → paid plan (week, 4-week, 12-week, quit-drinking / quit-smoking course) paid by card, Apple Pay or PayPal, then add-on offers; Premium also sold in-app; 4,511 reviews (every one read and hand-coded), 106 storefronts, 25 languages (English 2,171, Spanish 645, Russian 521, Ukrainian 261, French 243, German 196, Italian 110, Polish 107), 2020-05-12 → 2026-09-06, mean 3.55; listing (lookup API 2026-09-14): Health & Fitness / Productivity, age 12+, version 6.0.3 dated 2026-09-02, minimum iOS 15.0, 12 declared languages (AR, CS, EN, FR, DE, IT, JA, PL, PT, RU, ES, SV — Ukrainian and Kazakh absent), 'Subscription payments are charged to your iTunes account', 'Available plans: Monthly and Yearly', '300+ habit breakdowns' — web plans, add-ons and non-App-Store charges are not described; capabilities (verbatim): " + table("## 2.1 What the product is", 0) + " || public vs corpus by storefront (verbatim): " + table("## 2.2 What the store listing says", 0), "web funnel + in-app Premium", "mixed", "4,511 reviews; mean 3.55; US public 4.33 on 3,944", "none", "header", "app-specific", ["5936136499"])
c(2, "How to read this; Warnings 5, 6, 8; §1.1 table (verbatim); §1.2 table (verbatim); §1.3; §1.4; §1.5 table (verbatim); §1.6", "data-caveat", "Method and limits: non-exclusive counts; IDs plus date-order index #1…#4,511; read in date order in batches of 100 in original language; each batch re-asserted IDs at index and that every quoted fragment occurs in that review, with IDs filled from the index so they cannot drift; unknown codes rejected, 16 unions derived; build refuses to write on any non-verbatim quotation and asserts every stated trend direction; authenticity marks computed by rule, never used to drop reviews; files (verbatim) " + table("## 1.1 Files used", 0) + "; schema (verbatim) " + table("## 1.2 Schema actually present", 0) + "; reconciliation: 4,511 distinct, 0 duplicates, 1 repeat (storefront, author), 7 authors on >1 storefront, 106 country files match, manifest {1: 1519, 2: 51, 3: 73, 4: 175, 5: 2693}, mean 3.5480, 139 storefronts probed all complete, 163 edited, 212 with votes (max 19); bands (verbatim) " + table("## 1.5 Signal thresholds", 0) + "; limitations: selection (people write when charged and when prompted), inflation (E5 praise shares are upper bounds), purchases unverifiable, no version data, 2,340 non-English reviews, thin E1 (104) and E2 (196); storefront is not language (Ukraine writes Ukrainian, Russian, English; Israel's reviews mostly one-line Hebrew 5★ from E5); outcomes self-reported; not present: version per review, billing records, developer responses, device", "n/a", "mixed", "4,511 read; 106 storefronts; 20 eligible", "research", "method", "generalisable", ["13977689947","13518285285"])
c(3, "Warnings 1, 2; §0.3 table (verbatim); §9.H; §7.6 table (verbatim); §8.4; §8.10 #3; part 8 #3", "tactic", "The 2025 five-star record is not organic evidence: E5 (2025-04 → 2025-09) holds 2,363 of 4,511 reviews (52.38%, 394 a month vs 99 in E4 and 103 in E6, mean 4.03 vs 2.23 in the four months before and 3.34 after); five mechanical marks concentrate there (verbatim): " + table("## 0.3 The 2025 five-star record", 0) + " — identical one-liners posted the same day by generated names ('Es como compita que siempre está', mx, by 'Cheryln Kettlesingdmtptwre' and 'brealyn-todhunteraasmbcx'; 'ishlatish yoqimli', uz); three pairs of long identical US 5★ under different names in 2022-10 → 2023-01; a look-alike letter 'ọ' inserted to evade duplicate detection; 5★ is 74.8% of E5 vs 43.1% of everything else; the three busiest days (2025-09-23 42, 2025-08-29 33, 2025-08-31 33) all E5; sensitivity (verbatim): " + table("## 7.6 Sensitivity", 0) + " — without E5 the corpus is 41.8% billing complaint and 47.3% praise (mean 3.02); outcome: the public rating is not evidence of satisfaction; REV_DISTRUST 8 say positive reviews cannot be trusted; §8.4: stop requesting and templating reviews; research #3: who produced the E5 reviews", "suspected 5★ campaign Apr–Sep 2025", "5★-burst", "E5 2,363 (52.38%) @ 4.03; 238 generated names (230 in E5); 60 look-alike letter; 56 duplicate bodies in 28 groups; 1,885 short 5★", "dont", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12920984302","12921016298","13019377855","13019421337","11798385032","12665098547","13152464916"])
c(4, "§0.1; Warning 3; §3.3 table (verbatim); §8.1; §8.10 #2; part 8 #2", "must-never-break", "Billing and cancellation is the dominant complaint and it has one mechanism: U_BILLING_COMPLAINT 1,434 (31.79%, high-priority, mean 1.12, 2021-02-28 → 2026-09-06), in 1,384 of 1,570 1–2★ reviews (88.2%), across 87 storefronts — MON_SCAM 747 (16.56%), MON_EXTRA_CHARGE 632 (14.01%), MON_CANCEL_HARD 592 (13.12%), MON_WEB_BILLING 303 (6.72%), MON_RENEWAL_SHOCK 227 (5.03%), MON_CHARGE_AFTER_CANCEL 226 (5.01%), MON_ESCALATE 189 (4.19%); the chain: purchase on a website or in-funnel Apple Pay / PayPal / card → not in Apple's subscription list → the in-app 'Manage subscription' button opens that list anyway (BUG_MANAGE_SUB 60, 1.33%, from 2025-03-14) → cancellation by email only (MON_EMAIL 13) → support answers with offers (SUP_RETENTION 85, 1.88%) or not at all (SUP_NONE 352, 7.80%) → the charge recurs and the reviewer blocks the card or disputes it; 207 (4.59%) state both web billing and the failure to stop it: 'button directs to the App Store, but the actual subscription is handled outside via their website, to which access is blocked'; 'DOES NOT show their active subscription' (by, 7 votes); 'В AppStore вы не увидите эту подписку'; 'tuve que llamar al banco para dar orden de no pago'; the listing says payments are 'charged to your iTunes account'; billing codes (verbatim): " + table("## 3.3 Billing and cancellation", 0) + " — §8.1: route Manage subscription to wherever the subscription is billed, in-app cancellation for web subscriptions, stop billing on confirmation; research #2: how many active subscribers are billed off-store and can they see or cancel it", "web / Apple Pay / PayPal billing invisible to iOS; email-only cancel", "1★-burst", "1,434 (31.79%) 1.12; 88.2% of 1–2★; WEB_BILLING 303; MANAGE_SUB 60", "must-never-break", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12588412857","13269087947","14060777661","14402512848","11921513610","10422103648","12025277510","14043833740"])
c(5, "§0.2; §3.4 table (verbatim); §8.2; §8.10 #1; part 8 #1", "dont", "The purchase funnel sells on the next screen — a small plan, then $57: U_FUNNEL_SELL 178 (3.95%, very strong, mean 1.30, 2021-12-20 → 2026-08-22); MON_ONBOARD_SELL 37 (0.82%) offers during sign-up or right after payment where a tap adds a charge; the number 57 in 60 reviews (1.33%), 58 describing an unrequested extra charge, 2024-06-12 → 2026-09-01; intro price usually $6–10 for a week or month: 'along with the $9.92 charge, another $57 has been taken'; 'AUTOMATIQUEMENT vous venez d'acheter 3 PROGRAMMES SUPPLÉMENTAIRES, sans confirmation bancaire'; 'Кликнул на кнопку списало еще 57$ кликнул на другую кнопку еще 28$'; a decline button worded to shame — 'no I do not wish to improve my health' (NEG_DARK_PATTERN 1); 'Los botones estaban puestos de manera engañosa y confusa' (cl); funnel codes (verbatim): " + table("## 3.4 The funnel", 0) + " — §8.2: no charge without an explicit second confirmation, neutral 'No thanks', renewal price and date on the intro-plan screen and in a receipt email; research #1: what share of web purchasers are charged an add-on or renewal they dispute, and the chargeback rate", "post-payment one-tap add-ons; confirmshaming decline", "1★-burst", "FUNNEL_SELL 178 (3.95%) 1.30; ONBOARD_SELL 37; '57' in 60 reviews", "dont", "very strong", "generalisable", ["14361404522","14297661088","12418199607","14453772060","13819435071","8779339766","13600668706"])
c(6, "§0.2 renewal; §3.3; §6.19; §6.13", "must-never-break", "Intro plans that become large recurring charges: MON_RENEWAL_SHOCK 227 (5.03%, high-priority, mean 1.11, 2023-07-04 → 2026-09-03) — an intro plan that became a $39.95–$87 recurring charge; MON_BAIT 55 (1.22%, mean 1.05) advertised price not charged ('Ofrecen 4 semanas a 0.35 usd la semana y resulta que cobran 9.92usd por 7 días', ar); '€6.93 annual offer, €39.95 a week later' (it); 'Cada que entro a la app me da un costo diferente' (mx, MON_PRICE_SHIFT 6); MON_TRIAL_CHARGED 19 charged for a 'free' trial; MON_RECEIPT 17 no receipt or notice; 'it takes forever to figure out how much it costs a month' (MON_PRICE_UNCLEAR 4); 'every single month they keep charging me 79$' (il)", "cheap intro → auto-renew at $39.95–$87", "1★-burst", "RENEWAL_SHOCK 227 (5.03%) 1.11; BAIT 55 (1.22%) 1.05", "must-never-break", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["12910718578","12281581403","9349084473","13762280207","12895105557"])
c(7, "§3.3 escalation; §3.9 table (verbatim)", "timeline", "How reviewers try to stop it — escalation, not churn: MON_ESCALATE 189 (4.19%, very strong, mean 1.06) — blocking or cancelling the card, bank disputes and chargebacks, reports to Apple, police or regulators, lawyers ('raised a dispute'; 'со своим юристом'); REV_TIP 5 teach others to block payments in their bank app; PRIV_DATA 18 treat the stored card as the risk ('must delete your credit card after'); MON_LEGAL_CITE 2 ('comme le précise la loi'); churn and switching (verbatim): " + table("## 3.9 Churn, switching", 0) + " — 'Leaving is rarely the story; being unable to leave is': stated deletion 8 against 189 bank escalations; REV_ME_TOO 30 found the same complaint in other reviews first ('по отзывам- проблема частая')", "n/a", "1★-burst", "ESCALATE 189 (4.19%) 1.06; CHURN_DELETE 8; REV_ME_TOO 30", "must-never-break", "very strong", "generalisable", ["12757693206","11808696317","12192255446","14149306951","12780273120","14008782477"])
c(8, "§0.4; §3.5 tables (verbatim); §8.3; §8.9", "tactic", "Support moved from retention offers to named agents, and the praise is partly requested: until 2025 support is silent or answers a cancellation with an offer to stay (SUP_RETENTION 55 before 2025-10, SUP_NONE 273); in E6 (2025-10 →) PR_SUPPORT 62 of 1,238 (5.0%) against 9 in the 3,273 before; U_NAMED_AGENT 49 (1.09%, mean 4.49) — 'Nick' (29), then 'Emma', 'Michael', 'Sam' (20, all 2026); 14 of 45 E6 named-agent reviews report a refund, partial refund, free lifetime access or another retention gift ('Nick responded within hours. He canceled my subscription, issued a refund, and even upgraded me to lifetime access'); two texts show reviews being requested — 'My feedback goes to Michael who asked me to write it' (3★); 'Please post one review per day' (ng, 5★); earlier the same agent name: 'Nick keeps giving me offers I simply don't want' (1★); support codes and era table (verbatim): " + table("## 3.5 Support", 0) + " || " + table("## 3.5 Support", 1) + " — refunds received MON_REFUND_OK 27 (18 in E6), some in 1★ reviews that stay 1★; replies that seem automated SUP_AI_SUSPECT 5 ('the bot responds with nonsense'); outcome: fast, generous, named replies convert complainants into 5★ — §8.3 process the request before any retention offer, reply to every billing email, 'it should not depend on reaching a named agent'; §8.4 stop asking support contacts for reviews", "named agents give refunds / lifetime and ask for reviews", "5★-burst", "PR_SUPPORT E6 5.0% vs 9 before; NAMED_AGENT 49 @ 4.49; 14/45 gifted; SUP_NONE 352; RETENTION 85", "do", "meaningful", "generalisable", ["13995164939","13818735180","13977689947","13518285285","13005997779","14387826137","12628568220"])
c(9, "§0.5; §8.5; §8.10 #4; part 8 #4", "dont", "Ads for quitting drinking, smoking and vaping sell a product the app is not: USE_ADDICTION 24 (0.53%, emerging, mean 3.21, 2025-03-01 → 2026-09-01; 23 in E6) — the low-star ones (9) arrive from an Instagram / Facebook ad about alcohol, smoking or vaping, pay, and find a general habit checklist: 'This app advertises itself as a personalised program to help you reduce your drinking- it does nothing of the sort'; 'I downloaded this because of an IG ad focussed on reducing alcohol consumption but it's a habit tracker app'; 'there was nothing about vaping'; 'my first week of white knuckling sobriety, I found an ad for this app'; OUT_HARM 2 — 'Instead of helping me to quit drinking it's making me feel like drinking even more'; NEG_NOT_AS_ADVERTISED 59 (1.31%); the positive addiction reviews (14) are short; §8.5: addiction-themed ads should lead to a product that addresses the addiction, or not run; research #4: do addiction-ad cohorts retain or refund differently", "addiction ads → generic tracker", "1★-burst", "USE_ADDICTION 24 (0.53%) 3.21; NOT_AS_ADVERTISED 59 (1.31%) 1.27; OUT_HARM 2", "dont", "emerging", "generalisable", ["14363016127","13783722301","13453087689","13871480081","13824212239"])
c(10, "§0.6; §3.2 tables (verbatim); §8.9", "insight", "What genuinely works is a simple, attractive habit tracker: outside E5, 1,015 of 2,148 (47.3%) praise something specific — ease of use (PR_EASY 255), design (148), reminders (68), routines (78), tracking (119), the library (90), insights (63); the mechanism is low friction — a habit takes seconds to log, reminders prompt it, the library explains why ('large library of habits plus corresponding sources'); gentler than other trackers (PR_GRACE 75: 'doesn't make me feel bad when I mess up'); the two most-voted reviews (19 votes each, June 2023) are short tracker praise ('Best habit tracker I've come across'; 'Free Version is Great'); PR_FREE 26 say the free version is enough ('I find the basic non-paid version to be plenty'); all-review and outside-E5 praise (verbatim): " + table("### The tracker, the library and the reminders", 0) + " || " + table("### The tracker, the library and the reminders", 1) + " — §8.9 keep the simple check-off tracker, reminders and routines, the library with sources, and a useful free tier", "free tracker, library, reminders", "praise", "outside E5 praise 47.3%; PR_EASY 490 (10.86%) 4.91; PR_FREE 26", "build-free", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["10004391517","10005041599","13973006077","10980045764","9469982623","12665119947"])
c(11, "§3.2 outcomes table (verbatim)", "audience", "Outcomes and use contexts (verbatim): " + table("### Outcomes and use contexts", 0) + " — U_OUTCOME 520 (11.53%, high-priority, mean 4.95), 200 outside E5 (9.3%); reminders credited with getting out of bed ('even just getting out of bed seemed like an incredibly daunting task', 4 votes); professionals use it with clients ('As a Registered Dietitian', USE_COACH 3)", "n/a", "praise", "U_OUTCOME 520 (11.53%) 4.95; outside E5 200 (9.3%)", "none", "high-priority", "generalisable", ["11152761066","7038925744","13824212239"])
c(12, "§0.7; §3.7 table (verbatim); §8.7", "insight", "For the price the content reads as thin, generic and often in English: NEG_SIMPLE 97 (2.15%, meaningful, mean 1.40, 2021-09-11 → 2026-08-21) 'just a checklist' / nothing beyond other apps or common knowledge ('just a manual checklist'); NEG_CONTENT 33 (0.73%); NEG_AI_POOR 23 (0.51%) personalisation that feels generic ('I don't really see where the AI is supposed to be working'; 'No actual plan is provided'); NEG_AI_CONTENT 8 (0.18%, all E6) objections to AI-made design and text in the same era PR_AI is praised (15 of 20); together 137 (3.04%) find it thin, 32 also object to price; NEG_INCLUSIVE 2 'not designed with women in mind at all'; content codes (verbatim): " + table("## 3.7 Content, personalisation", 0) + " — §8.7: test a demonstrably personal plan (schedule, sequence, adaptive check-ins) against the library", "paid plan = the free library", "complaint", "NEG_SIMPLE 97 (2.15%) 1.40; thin union 137 (3.04%)", "research", "meaningful", "generalisable", ["7795806947","9561312304","12750177813","10845943293","12110643224"])
c(13, "§0.7 language; §3.7; §8.5", "dont", "Language gaps after ads in the user's language: NEG_LANG 32 (0.71%, emerging, mean 2.06) — an interface in the user's language with videos, notifications or the whole app in English, often after an ad in their language: 'Интерфейс на русском, а вот все видео на английском'; 'Реклама була українською мовою' (the ad was in Ukrainian); 'La app está en español pero las notificaciones llegan en inglés'; language errors in the Polish interface; Ukrainian (261 reviews) and Kazakh (47) are not declared listing languages although ua and kz are the second- and third-largest storefronts; §8.5: do not advertise in a language the content is not in; declare and localise Ukrainian and Kazakh if those storefronts are targeted", "ads in Ukrainian; app content English", "complaint", "NEG_LANG 32 (0.71%) 2.06", "dont", "emerging", "generalisable", ["12244660753","12284974864","9452455789","13951278357"])
c(14, "§3.6 table (verbatim)", "must-never-break", "Defects (verbatim): " + table("## 3.6 Defects", 0) + " — small next to billing; two matter: the 'Manage subscription' dead end (60) and the launch failure of 2023-01-04 when 13 reviews arrived in one day, 12 saying the app would not load ('App won't even open'; 'the app support link on the App Store also doesn't work'); BUG_PURCHASE 18 paid access never unlocked; BUG_LOGIN 41 login failures often after a web purchase; BUG_LINK 15 broken link or support address", "launch failure 2023-01-04; manage-sub dead end", "1★-burst", "MANAGE_SUB 60; LOGIN 41; LAUNCH 37; PURCHASE 18", "must-never-break", "meaningful", "generalisable", ["9456046627","9471340530","10934083454"])
c(15, "§3.8 table (verbatim); §8.8", "feature", "Unmet needs (verbatim): " + table("## 3.8 Unmet needs", 0) + " — U_REQ_ANY 89 (1.97%, mean 3.38) — few because most reviewers are not using the app long enough to want more; long-term users ask for Apple Health integration and automatic tracking (REQ_HEALTH 9, REQ_AUTO_TRACK 2), habit ordering and schedules (REQ_REORDER 7: 'sort those habits chronologically'; REQ_SCHEDULE 5), a sick day ('flagging a day as sick day'), and a real free trial before any charge (REQ_TRIAL 4); §8.8: Apple Health and habit ordering as an experiment to raise free-user retention", "absent", "complaint", "REQ_ANY 89 (1.97%) 3.38; HEALTH 9; REORDER 7", "research", "weak", "generalisable", ["9469982623","10005041599"])
